Happy New Year!  @lavalamp - I made a number of changes to the code over the holidays after your comments.  Hopefully the language is is lot more consistent and cleaned up.  I've also found the additional logging extremely useful in debugging some issues I was seeing in client code along the way, which helped me discover a race that can occur between an item being processed and the nextReadyAt timer being updated and the test stepping the fake clock forward.  This could also happen with the old code but with a lot less going on it would have been a lot less likely!  For this reason, I have moved some updating of the nextReadyAt timer inside of the processArrivingEntry() so that we ensure it is done before a synchronous call returns control back to the tests.  Having done this it seemed reasonable to want to only update the timer when it is needed (i.e. the head item in the 'waiting' queue is changed) and not every time around the loop.

